#
# direnv entry point. `direnv allow` once, and every shell opened in this tree gets the pinned
# toolchains from flake.nix instead of whatever the host happens to have installed.
#
# This is the same devShell CI uses, which is the point: the class of bug where a build passes
# locally and fails in CI is usually a toolchain the developer had and the runner did not.
# nix.conf at the root already enables the flakes experimental features this needs.

# The default devShell — bazelisk, buildifier, buf, go, nodejs_22, pnpm, protobuf, python312,
# ruff, uv and the pinned Rust toolchain from tools/build/nix/toolchains/rust.nix.
#
# For the lint and terraform lanes' extra tooling (actionlint, shellcheck, yamllint, terraform,
# cargo-deny), use `nix develop .#ci` directly rather than switching this line — the ci shell
# is heavier and pulls terraform, which is BUSL-licensed and needs the allowUnfree predicate
# flake.nix sets for it.
use flake

# nix-direnv caches the shell derivation so the second `cd` into the tree is instant rather
# than re-evaluating the flake. Falls through harmlessly if it is not installed; without it
# `use flake` still works, just slowly.
if ! has nix_direnv_version; then
  log_status "nix-direnv not found — shell evaluation will be slow. See https://github.com/nix-community/nix-direnv"
fi

export MINDCLADE_REPO_ROOT="$PWD"

# Matches the shellHook in flake.nix. Set here as well because a shell entered through direnv
# and one entered through `nix develop` must not differ: PYTHONNOUSERSITE stops a stray
# ~/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages shadowing a pinned dependency, which presents as a
# version mismatch in a package nobody in this repository declared.
export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1

# Local secrets, if any. .env is gitignored precisely because it is the one place a real
# credential plausibly lands in this repo (see .gitignore); dotenv_if_exists loads it without
# making a checkout without one fail.
dotenv_if_exists .env
